                    <child>
                      <object class="GtkCheckButton" id="combine_generic">
                        <property name="label" translatable="yes">Present as generic "Oversteer Combined Wheel"</property>
                        <property name="visible">True</property>
                        <property name="can-focus">True</property>
                        <property name="receives-default">False</property>
                        <property name="tooltip-text" translatable="yes">Off: the combined device keeps the wheel's own identity so games apply their built-in profile. On: a generic device set up as a custom wheel in the game. Needed for Forza Horizon 6, which drops force feedback for a recognised wheel in a custom profile but keeps it for a generic one. Forza will not navigate menus from an unknown device, so keep a gamepad or keyboard for menus.</property>
